The carve-out lives here rather than in LICENSE because GitHub's licence
detector compares LICENSE against the canonical MIT text and reports
NOASSERTION when anything is appended to it. An undetected licence is read
downstream as no licence at all: the MCP directory that scores this server
graded the repository F on licence and disabled its install button while these
two paragraphs sat at the bottom of the MIT text.
